    short: 'A durable waiting line that separates the producer of work from its consumer.',
    definition: 'A Message Queue stores messages until a consumer can process them. The producer can finish quickly, while consumers process work independently and at a rate they can sustain.',
    why: 'Synchronous chains make one slow or unavailable service block everyone upstream. A queue absorbs spikes and isolates failures.',
    useWhen: ['Work can happen after the original request finishes', 'Producers and consumers should scale separately', 'You need retry and failure handling around background work'],
